{{Quote|Sistros, one of the four ancient philosophers of Dwartii. I keep it for sentimental value.|Emperor Palpatine, on his statue of Sistros|<ref name="Tarkin">[[Tarkin (novel)|''Tarkin'']]</ref>}}
'''Sistros Nevet'''<ref name="Galaxy'sEdge">{{GEAttr|Dok-Ondar's Den of Antiquities}}</ref> was a [[Gender|female]]<ref name="SW100O" /> member of the [[Four Sages of Dwartii]],<ref name="TVE" /> ancient lawgivers from the dawn of the [[Galactic Republic]]. Sistros was involved in the formation of the [[Galactic Constitution|Republic's original constitution]].<ref name="Propaganda">''[[Star Wars Propaganda: A History of Persuasive Art in the Galaxy]]''</ref> A cold and calculating [[Nouanese]] [[minister]] and lawmaker, Sistros was known for being an emotionless ruler in life, accused of using<ref name="SW100O" /> her<ref name="Inside Intel" /> power during the Republic's formation for her own selfish ends.<ref name="SW100O" />

[[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]] admired this [[Timeline of galactic history|historical]] [[philosopher]] throughout his [[Politics|political]] career. As the [[Senator]] of [[Naboo]], he recommended to [[Supreme Chancellor]] [[Finis Valorum]] to use the image of Sistros as the centerpiece of the [[Millennial Celebration Invitation|invitations]] for the celebration marking the [[Galactic Republic]]'s [[Millennium|millennial]] anniversary.<ref name="Propaganda" /> During his own tenure as Supreme Chancellor, Palpatine kept a [[bronzium]] statue depicting Sistros as a [[cloak]]ed figure in [[Emperor's office|his office]].<ref name="Episode II">{{Film|II}}</ref> After he became [[Galactic Emperor]] at the [[19 BBY|end]] of the [[Clone Wars]], Palpatine moved to [[Pinnacle Room|new quarters]] in the [[Imperial Palace]], taking with him the Sistros statue,<ref name="Tarkin" /> which had a [[neuranium]] coating under the outer [[bronze]], and hiding [[Darth Sidious' lightsabers|one]] of his [[Sith]] [[lightsaber]]s inside it.<ref name="Complete Locations">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref>

